# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the two values below.
# .env.local is already in .gitignore, so it will never be committed or
# pushed to GitHub — that's exactly what you want for a secret API key.

# 1. Sign up free at https://resend.com (no credit card required for the
#    free tier: 100 emails/day, 3,000/month, plenty for a contact/booking form).
# 2. Create an API key: Dashboard -> API Keys -> Create API Key.
# 3. Paste it here:
RESEND_API_KEY=re_your_api_key_here

# 4. The email address YOU want to receive contact and booking messages at.
#    This can be any real inbox you check — Gmail, Outlook, whatever you use.
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=you@example.com

# That's it — both forms are already wired up to use these. After setting
# them, restart the dev server (Ctrl+C, then npm run dev) so Next.js picks
# up the new values.
#
# One more step for when you deploy (e.g. to Vercel): add these same two
# variables in your hosting provider's dashboard under
# Project Settings -> Environment Variables, since .env.local only works
# locally and is never uploaded anywhere.
#
# Note on the sender address: emails currently send from
# "onboarding@resend.dev", Resend's shared testing address, which works
# immediately with no setup. If you want emails to instead say
# "from @geleglamzzz.com", that requires verifying your domain in the
# Resend dashboard (Domains -> Add Domain) and adding a few DNS records —
# not required to get started, just an option later for a more polished
# sender name.
